The Chrome extension (extension/) ships no third-party code: it is compiled with
plain tsc and the release zip holds only its own scripts, pages and icons. Its npm
packages (TypeScript, ESLint, Vitest, Playwright, Prettier and their dependencies)
are build and test tools under their own licenses (MIT, Apache-2.0 or BSD) and are
not distributed. The crates the bridge adds next to tungstenite (sha2, getrandom)
are MIT OR Apache-2.0.

